put.summary:
Replaces the account's (group's) compute policy with the supplied set
of grants. Each grant must be within the organization's current policy;
out-of-subset entries are rejected per-cluster.

jwt.description:
jwt is a fresh admin token minted for the admin identified in the
caller's `act` claim. The UI proxy stores it in an HttpOnly cookie;
no other consumer should read this field directly.

threads.description:
threads dictates if hardware threads of allocated cores are exposed
to the job container. When unset, the job inherits the defaults value;
an explicit true or false overrides it.
